summary:
- topic: Summer Learning Programs
  text: The district successfully ran various summer programs for students, including
    ESL, Extended School Year, Elementary Summer Academy, and a High School Summer
    Academy that helped students recover 33 academic credits. Staff also engaged in
    extensive professional development on topics like math strategies, reading instruction,
    and positive behavioral interventions.
- topic: District Goals and Strategic Planning
  text: The Superintendent introduced the 2024-2025 Pillars & Priorities, adding a
    new 'Planning' pillar to focus on strategic planning, boundaries, and configurations.
    The new district theme, 'Together We Grow,' was also unveiled, emphasizing belonging
    and continuous improvement for all.
- topic: School Safety and Security Updates
  text: The Director of Operations and Safety reported on significant safety accomplishments,
    including new standard response procedures, security audits, and physical security
    upgrades at multiple buildings. Ongoing work includes customizing reunification
    plans for each school and addressing door and camera issues at the middle school.
- topic: Freedom of Access Act Training
  text: The Assistant Superintendent provided an annual review of the Freedom of Access
    Act for board members, distributing training materials and offering individual
    follow-up calls to ensure compliance and understanding of public information requirements.
- topic: Personnel and Community Donations
  text: The board approved several new personnel elections, including a Director of
    Mental and Behavioral Health, a School Psychologist, and an Assistant Director
    of Instructional Support. Generous donations from Eagle Associates, the South
    Portland/Cape Elizabeth Community Chamber, and Pape Subaru were also accepted.
- topic: Policy Review and Approval
  text: Eighteen policies, including those related to learning results, student activities
    funds, bonded employees, hazard reporting, school closings, staff conduct, and
    public access, underwent a second reading and were approved by the board.
